       sseett__aallll
           Set the limits for which no value is specified in the configuration
           file to the one from the process with the PID 1. Please note that
           if the init process is systemd these limits will not be the kernel
           default limits and this option should not be used.

       uuttmmpp__eeaarrllyy
           Some broken applications actually allocate a utmp entry for the
           user before the user is admitted to the system. If some of the
           services you are configuring PAM for do this, you can selectively
           use this module argument to compensate for this behavior and at the
           same time maintain system-wide consistency with a single
           limits.conf file.

       nnooaauuddiitt
           Do not report exceeded maximum logins count to the audit subsystem.

